      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<table style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">\n\t<thead>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<th>Option</th>\n\t\t\t<th>Word</th>\n\t\t\t<th>Possible/Not</th>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</thead>\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>1</td>\n\t\t\t<td>Acuse</td>\n\t\t\t<td>(Letter <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">E</span> not present)</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>2</td>\n\t\t\t<td>Curse</td>\n\t\t\t<td> (Letter <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">R</span> and <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">E</span> not present)</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>3</td>\n\t\t\t<td>Cure</td>\n\t\t\t<td>(Letter <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">R</span> and <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">E</span> not present)</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>4</td>\n\t\t\t<td>Caution</td>\n\t\t\t<td> (All letters present in ACCUSATION)</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Thus, <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">CAUTION</span> can be formed from the letters of <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">ACCUSATION</span>.</p>\n",
